    {
      "id": "h1fu16k",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Introduction"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Asexual reproduction involves a single parent producing genetically identical offspring without gametes.",
        "Sexual reproduction requires the fusion of male and female gametes to create genetic diversity.",
        "The male reproductive system produces sperm, while the female reproductive system produces ova and supports fetal development.",
        "The menstrual cycle is a monthly reproductive cycle in human females regulated by hormones.",
        "Pollination transfers pollen from anther to stigma, preceding fertilization in plants."
      ],
      "id": "f7a7r5u"
    },
    {
      "type": "statStrip",
      "stats": [
        {
          "label": "Modes of Reproduction",
          "value": "2 Types",
          "icon": "book"
        },
        {
          "label": "Average Menstrual Cycle",
          "value": "28 Days",
          "icon": "clock"
        },
        {
          "label": "Key Processes in Plants",
          "value": "Pollination & Fertilization",
          "icon": "check"
        },
        {
