    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "tow0mq0",
      "content": "Reproduction is the biological process by which organisms produce new individuals of the same species. It ensures continuity of life on earth. Reproduction is of two main types: Asexual and Sexual."
    },
    {
      "id": "ohkyu56",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "2. Asexual Reproduction"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "k3blovv",
      "content": "• Only one parent is involved."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "i16s29d",
      "content": "• Offspring are genetically identical (clones)."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "bzw8l2r",
      "content": "• Rapid method of reproduction."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "uypi7i1",
      "content": "• Common in unicellular organisms and plants."
    },
    {
      "id": "9i9zob9",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "3. Types of Asexual Reproduction"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "xevayhc",
      "content": "• Binary Fission – Amoeba, Paramecium."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "cw8rl8h",
      "content": "• Multiple Fission – Plasmodium."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "i5abdc9",
      "content": "• Budding – Yeast, Hydra."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "4yg28g9",
      "content": "• Fragmentation – Spirogyra."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "yf2w9m1",
      "content": "• Spore Formation – Rhizopus."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "q5zzmt5",
      "content": "• Vegetative Propagation – Potato, Bryophyllum."
    },
    {
      "id": "ww6f2so",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "4. Sexual Reproduction"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "pb0o1bl",
      "content": "• Involves two parents (male and female)."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "9mtfz6s",
      "content": "• Gametes are formed (sperm and ovum)."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "mipkb0v",
      "content": "• Fertilization produces zygote."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "yvozi7v",
      "content": "• Offspring show variation."
    },
    {
      "id": "k1cweb1",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "5. Human Reproductive System – Male"
    },
    {
      "type": "pullQuote",
      "content": "CHAPTER 7: REPRODUCTION",
      "id": "em5bq84"
    },
