    {
      "id": "q542x94",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "7. Menstrual Cycle"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "8moytob",
      "content": "• Occurs every 28 days (average)."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "8scbr3c",
      "content": "• Day 1–5: Menstrual phase (bleeding)."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "qpxe0vq",
      "content": "• Day 6–14: Follicular phase (egg maturation)."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "2o8ustq",
      "content": "• Day 14: Ovulation."
    },
    {
      "type": "comparisonTable",
      "headers": [
        "Feature",
        "Asexual Reproduction",
        "Sexual Reproduction"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "Number of Parents",
          "One parent",
          "Two parents"
        ],
        [
          "Gamete Formation",
          "Not involved",
          "Involved (Sperm and Ovum)"
        ],
        [
          "Genetic Variation",
          "Clones (Identical to parent)",
          "Varied offspring"
        ]
      ],
      "id": "g8bmm61"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "lcskevn",
      "content": "• Day 15–28: Luteal phase."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "m0dg1xt",
      "content": "• If fertilization does not occur, cycle repeats."
    },
    {
      "id": "9uy7i1k",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "8. Pollination"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "lzeqoil",
      "content": "• Transfer of pollen from anther to stigma."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "0voshps",
      "content": "• Self-pollination – Same flower."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "5xaxbuy",
      "content": "• Cross-pollination – Different plant."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "2666oym",
      "content": "• Agents: Wind, Water, Insects, Animals."
    },
    {
      "id": "9b32on9",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "9. Fertilization"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "njpkpe5",
      "content": "• Fusion of male and female gametes."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "sausivb",
      "content": "• Produces zygote."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "u6hlhul",
      "content": "• In plants, occurs inside ovule."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ds0cbvc",
      "content": "• In humans, occurs in fallopian tube."
    },
    {
      "id": "3phx9ts",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "10. Types of Reproduction in Plants"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "xyinapu",
      "content": "• Vegetative Propagation – Through roots, stems, leaves."
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Site of fertilization in human females is the Fallopian Tube (Oviduct).",
        "Types of asexual reproduction (Binary Fission, Budding, Fragmentation) are frequently asked in RRB and SSC exams.",
        "Differentiate clearly between cross-pollination and self-pollination mechanisms."
      ],
      "id": "ewkstuf"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "zfl2rtd",
      "content": "• Spore Formation – Ferns, Mosses."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "h4mu8pt",
      "content": "• Sexual Reproduction – Through flowers and seeds."
    },
    {
      "id": "tiacn3a",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "11. Quick Revision Points (RRB Focus)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "8swrcqo",
      "content": "1. Asexual reproduction produces clones."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "2jsx6tq",
      "content": "2. Binary fission in Amoeba."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "5xy8jkp",
      "content": "3. Fertilization occurs in fallopian tube."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "6w4r3x7",
      "content": "4. Ovulation occurs around 14th day."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "aljfrqe",
      "content": "5. Self and cross pollination are two types."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ykx38us",
      "content": "6. Zygote develops into embryo."
    }
  ],
